#!/usr/bin/env rexx
/*
   author:  Rony G. Flatscher

   name:    javafx_update_GUI-from-non-GUI-thread.rxj

   date:    2018-07-19

   purpose: this JavaFX GUI application demonstrates how to update a GUI object (a Label)
            from a non-GUI thread using the methods of the public class .FxGuiThread defined
            in BSF.CLS

   license: Apache License 2.0 (see at bottom)

   invoke:

         rexx javafx_01.rex
         rexxj.{cmd|sh} javafx_01.rex

   needs: ooRexx 4.1 or higher, and BSF4ooRexx 6.00 or highter

*/


-- >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
/*
   Name:    "2-080_ShowCount.rxj"

   Invoke:  "rexx Showcount.rxj"
                or
            "rexxj Showcount.rxj" (Windows)
                or
            "rexxj.sh Showcount.rxj" (Unix)

   Purpose:  creates a simple window (Frame) with a Label and a Button. ... ??? ...
             the number of times the button was pressed

   Date:     2018-07-19

   Changed: ---

   license:

